# s3-fglease-rust: the foreground-lease owner thread lives in mixdog_window.node (native/mixdog-window/src/foreground_lease.rs).
# Lines for files s3-fglease-rust does not own; the lead applies them after the wave.

[native/mixdog-window/Cargo.toml]
# The s1-mica dependency lines (napi, napi-derive, napi-build) are required, and the napi feature must include
# napi4 (napi6 as in deferred-g1.md does): ThreadsafeFunction (the lease thread reports a lease's end to JavaScript).
# No other crate: foreground_lease.rs uses std and raw-dylib user32/kernel32 only.
# cargo test in native/mixdog-window runs the lease unit tests (a stand-in for user32, no real lock is taken).

[apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts]
# At startup, where micaLibraryPath(...) is first computed for nativeMica, also call
#   setForegroundLeaseLibrary(micaLibraryPath({ isPackaged: app.isPackaged, resourcesPath: process.resourcesPath, appPath: app.getAppPath() }));
# (import from './computer/backend/foreground-lock-host'), before the first lease ask can arrive
# (host/computer-lease.ts processForegroundLock and computer/host/powershell-host.ts). Windows only. Without the call the
# lease owner reports "the path of mixdog_window.node was not set" once at error level and answers every ask unavailable.

[apps/desktop/src/main/host/computer-lease.test.mjs]
# Not owned by s3-fglease-rust and broken by it: it imports leaseThreadStarter (removed with the koffi worker thread) and the
# fixture fixtures/fake-lease-native.cjs. Pass a runtime built with nativeForegroundLease(() => fakeModule) (the fake
# module of foreground-lock-host.test.mjs: leaseStart/leaseRequest/leaseEnd/leaseGone/leaseDispose/leaseUnlock) and drop the
# SharedArrayBuffer counters; lease deadlines and unlock retries are tested in Rust now.

[apps/desktop/src/main/computer/backend/fixtures/fake-lease-native.cjs]
# Delete (only the two tests above used it).

[apps/desktop/src/main/computer/backend/source-bundle.test.mjs]
# The case at line ~55 bundles foreground-lock-host.ts and compares LEASE_THREAD_SOURCE with
# loadComputerSource('foreground-lease-thread.cjs'): both are gone. Drop that case, or keep the bundle check without
# the LEASE_THREAD_SOURCE assertion.

[apps/desktop/scripts/computer-source-assets.mjs]
# backendModule regex: remove foreground-lock-host from the list (it no longer calls loadComputerSource).

[apps/desktop/src/main/computer/backend/sources/MixForegroundLock.cs]
# Comment only: "(foreground-lease-thread.cjs)" -> "(native/mixdog-window foreground_lease.rs)", lines 2 and 39.

[native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_flip.rs]
# Nothing: no protocol method is added.
